s.twimg.com/media/HW3k_X2XcAAFOcs.jpg", "height": 654}], "linkEmbed": false, "replies": 14, "created": 1794426076000, "id": "2120602782084579641", "video": false, "poll": false, "user": {"profilePicture": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2119629772850438144/IZZFDXUO_normal.jpg", "displayName": "Rabbi of Peace \u2721\ufe0f", "username": "RabbiOfPeace"}, "content": "Did you know a U.S. Army engineer leaked nuclear and missile secrets to a foreign nation, but wasn't caught for 20+ years?\n\nBen-Ami Kadish smuggled classified blueprints on nukes, F-15s, and Patriot missiles out of a military arsenal from 1979 to 1985.\n\nHey @Grok, in few words", "parentTweet": false, "likes": 123}}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "text", "uuid": "1ATodgUDTf", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 49, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8935333, "raw_content": "Veterans Day \u2013 Quick facts:\r\n\r\nDate: Always November 11, regardless of the day of the week. \r\n\r\nStatus: A federal holiday; most government agencies and USPS are closed. \r\n\r\nDistinction: Honors all veterans (living or dead), unlike Memorial Day which honors those who died in service. \r\n\r\nObservance: Includes parades, ceremonies, and commercial discounts for military personnel.", "author": "Bullet3250", "created": 1794405265712, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "PresElectKekPede", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "Veterans Day", "last_comment_created": 1794417249554, "content": "<p>Veterans Day \u2013 Quick facts:</p>\n<p>Date: Always November 11, regardless of the day of the week.</p>\n<p>Status: A federal holiday; most government agencies and USPS are closed.</p>\n<p>Distinction: Honors all veterans (living or dead), unlike Memorial Day which honors those who died in service.</p>\n<p>Observance: Includes parades, ceremonies, and commercial discounts for military personnel.</p>\n", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 2, "score_up": 49, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "text", "uuid": "1ATodgV2gs", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 24, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8935642, "raw_content": "Saying immigration is the cause and \"look at all the immigrants across Texas\" is a narrative, a psyop to cover the steal.  \n\n\n1. two years isn't enough to have that level of a swing.\n\n 2. ICE and deportations are up since Trump got in office as is less coming in. Overall Texas is bad off, but the comparison is Talafeako vs 2 years prior\n\n3. MIdterms are low turnout for citizens who have a vested interest in this country. Do you really believe illegal immigrants get in and within 2 years get all civic minded for a friggin midterm? \n\n4. James Talarico as a candidate is actually evidence they cheated. Why? If you were trying to win a race in Texas legitimately, you would pick a moderate democrat. If you KNOW because you're going to cheat that your guy is getting in, then pick the most radical homo you can think of.\n\nThe fact they ran with talarico in Texas means they knew they were going to install someone, as he's radical by California standards.\n\nNow if you want to say fraud by using illegal immigrants as a cover then that's something different, but then it becomes about fraud and not about people legitimately voting.", "author": "StaticNoise2", "created": 1794419226074, "profile_picture": "iPSqIDDiZC8M", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "Hunters_underwear", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "Saying Texas went blue because of immigrants is bullcrap; here's why", "last_comment_created": 1794427135235, "content": "<p>Saying immigration is the cause and &quot;look at all the immigrants across Texas&quot; is a narrative, a psyop to cover the steal.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p>two years isn't enough to have that level of a swing.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>ICE and deportations are up since Trump got in office as is less coming in. Overall Texas is bad off, but the comparison is Talafeako vs 2 years prior</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>MIdterms are low turnout for citizens who have a vested interest in this country. Do you really believe illegal immigrants get in and within 2 years get all civic minded for a friggin midterm?</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>James Talarico as a candidate is actually evidence they cheated. Why? If you were trying to win a race in Texas legitimately, you would pick a moderate democrat. If you KNOW because you're going to cheat that your guy is getting in, then pick the most radical homo you can think of.</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p>The fact they ran with talarico in Texas means they knew they were going to install someone, as he's radical by California standards.</p>\n<p>Now if you want to say fraud by using illegal immigrants as a cover then that's something different, but then it becomes about fraud and not about people legitimately voting.</p>\n", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 25, "score_up": 2